<div class="sop-meta">
  <div><strong>Trigger</strong> Bi-weekly send (Tuesday 9am local)</div>
  <div><strong>Owner</strong> Jon</div>
  <div><strong>Time</strong> 60-90 min per send</div>
  <div><strong>Output</strong> Newsletter sent to 3 list segments; opens/clicks logged</div>
</div>

<h2>List structure</h2>
<p>Three segments. Send the same body to all three but with a tailored intro paragraph.</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Warm leads.</strong> Audit recipients, discovery-call no-shows, "later this year" responses. Goal: re-engage. Largest segment.</li>
  <li><strong>Past clients.</strong> Anyone who has launched a site with me and is still active or recently offboarded. Goal: stay top-of-mind for retention, upsell, and referral. Smallest segment, highest value.</li>
  <li><strong>Partners.</strong> Tier 3 networking contacts, business coaches, agencies, accountants. Goal: keep them informed about who I serve well, so referrals stay accurate.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Newsletter template (one tip + one ship + one ask)</h2>

<h3>Tip</h3>
<p>One specific, useful observation drawn from a recent audit, build, or post. 2-4 sentences. Plain language. Always teach something concrete the reader can use without me.</p>

<h3>Ship</h3>
<p>One thing I shipped recently, a new blog post, a new sample site, an updated service page, a public changelog entry. 1-2 sentences + link. Demonstrates the agency is active and improving.</p>

<h3>Ask</h3>
<p>One soft CTA. Not the same one every time. Rotate:</p>
<ul>
  <li>"Got a friend in [trade] still on Wix? Forward this."</li>
  <li>"If your own site is on the list of things-to-fix, the free audit is open."</li>
  <li>"Working on something seasonal? <a href="/events/">Here is the campaign that fits.</a>" (only when an event is active)</li>
  <li>"Heard from a client this week with a great review, <a href="/results/">the public stats are here</a>."</li>
</ul>

<h2>Compliance</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>CAN-SPAM (U.S.):</strong> Physical postal address in every send. One-click unsubscribe in every send. Honor unsubscribes within 10 business days (in practice: same day).</li>
  <li><strong>CASL (Canada):</strong> Express consent at signup or implied consent (recent business relationship within 24 months). Document the consent source per subscriber.</li>
  <li><strong>GDPR:</strong> Double opt-in for any EU subscriber. Standard practice: send confirm-link on signup, do not add to list until clicked.</li>
  <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> Privacy policy linked in every send. Data retention: drop unengaged subscribers (no opens in 6 months) after one win-back attempt.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Lead magnets to drive signups</h2>
<p>Newsletter signups come from three places. The lead magnets at each:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Free 5-point audit (<code>/audit/</code>).</strong> Audit recipients are auto-added with consent at submission.</li>
  <li><strong>Blog post bottom CTAs.</strong> "Liked this? Get one tip a week, no spam." Drives opt-ins from organic search traffic.</li>
  <li><strong>Downloadable PDF.</strong> "10-point pre-launch website checklist" or similar. Email-gated. The single highest-converting magnet for service-business owners.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Steps for each send</h2>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Tuesday 8am: pull the three components (tip, ship, ask).</li>
  <li>Draft the body. Read aloud once; cut every word that does not earn its place.</li>
  <li>Tailor the intro paragraph for each of the three segments.</li>
  <li>Set subject line. A/B test where the platform supports it.</li>
  <li>Schedule for 9am local recipient time (split-send if needed for timezones).</li>
  <li>Wednesday: pull the open/click report. Log to the running spreadsheet.</li>
  <li>Thursday: respond to any replies (every reply gets a personal answer; this is the single most valuable habit).</li>
</ul>

<h2>KPIs to track</h2>
<ul>
  <li>List size by segment.</li>
  <li>Open rate by segment (target: 30%+ for clients, 20%+ for warm leads, 25%+ for partners).</li>
  <li>Click rate (target: 5%+ overall).</li>
  <li>Replies per send (qualitative; this is the leading indicator of conversion).</li>
  <li>Discovery calls / audits attributable to the newsletter (the lagging indicator).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Common issues</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Open rate dropping.</strong> Subject lines are stale or list is stale. Run a re-engagement sequence; drop unengaged subscribers.</li>
  <li><strong>Cadence slips to monthly.</strong> Bi-weekly is the floor that produces results. Monthly is too thin to stay top-of-mind.</li>
  <li><strong>Body gets long.</strong> Three sections, three paragraphs. If a send goes over 250 words, cut.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Exit criteria per send</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Sent on Tuesday 9am local.</li>
  <li>Replies answered within 48 hours.</li>
  <li>Open and click rates logged.</li>
  <li>Any unsubscribes processed; any signups confirmed.</li>
</ul>
